# SemText sem-table — six display modes on one design sheet
# House style shared with the other tag prompts (minimal-tech light theme,
# dark slate canvas). One example page per display mode, in one frame:
# plain sortable (default), filter, sticky internal-scroll, comparison
# first-column stick, class-form alias, and the no-scripts plain table.
#
# NOTE on the attached reference renders: the snapshot harness masks every
# position:sticky element page-wide, so the header row and pinned first
# column are MISSING from some references. The design intent — and the
# graded requirement — is that enhanced panels ALWAYS show a legible
# header row (sort arrows on sortable columns) and the comparison panel
# shows its first column pinned. Do not copy the masked state.
schema: "0.4"
id: sem-table-ux-design
type: image
quality: high
product_targets:
  - semtext.dev
tags:
  - semtext
  - sem-table
  - ux-design
  - reference

prompt:
  text: |
    UX design sheet for the SemText `<sem-table>` element: a 3x2 grid of
    SIX labeled example pages, each a small card-framed data table in the
    minimal-tech-light theme on a dark slate canvas (bg #0f172a, surface
    #1e293b, fg #e2e8f0, accent #60a5fa, hairline #334155 borders, mono
    uppercase caption labels). Every enhanced panel shows a REAL header
    row with legible column labels.

    Panel 1 — caption "SORTABLE (default)". A 3-row table, caption
    "Token lifetimes", columns TOKEN / LIFETIME / ROTATES. Header labels
    in small caps; each sortable header carries a tiny neutral up/down
    arrow pair. The LIFETIME header is the active sort: accent-colored
    label with a single filled down-arrow, and the three body rows
    visibly ordered by duration (15 min, 7 days, 30 days). No filter
    box, no chrome bar — with nothing but sort the element shows only
    the table.

    Panel 2 — caption "FILTER". The "Active sessions" table (3 rows,
    columns DEVICE / LAST SEEN / REGION) inside a slim chrome bar: a
    labelled search input reading "Filter rows" on the left, a muted
    status text "3 rows" on the right. Header labels are plain — no
    sort arrows on this panel.

    Panel 3 — caption "STICKY". A 10-row "Recent deploys" table capped
    at a fixed height: an internal scrollbar on the table frame's right
    edge with the thumb pulled mid-way, five body rows visible, rows 6+
    fading under the frame bottom — and the HEADER ROW still fully
    visible at the top of the scroll area (surface background, hairline
    below), pinned over the scrolled body. This is the whole point of
    the panel: header stays, body scrolls inside its own frame.

    Panel 4 — caption "COMPARISON". A narrow phone-width frame with a
    6-column "Hosting plans" table scrolling horizontally INSIDE its own
    frame (a short horizontal scrollbar under the body): the PLAN
    column (Dev / Team / Scale) is PINNED at the left edge — opaque
    surface background, a hairline shadow at its right boundary — while
    the ROWS / STORAGE / BACKUPS columns slide beneath it, one column
    visibly cut mid-glyph by the pinned edge. Header row fully visible.

    Panel 5 — caption "CLASS FORM". Pixel-identical to panel 1 (same
    "Token lifetimes" table, chrome-less, arrows on headers): the alias
    authoring form renders exactly like the element form. Same table,
    same arrows, same order.

    Panel 6 — caption "NO SCRIPTS". The authored table bare: caption
    "Token lifetimes", plain small-caps header labels with NO arrows,
    three rows in authored order, no chrome bar, no search input, no
    scrollbar. Everything readable, nothing interactive, nothing hidden.

    Typography: clean system sans (Inter-like), 13-14px table text,
    1.5 line height, captions in mono uppercase. Consistent card radius
    and spacing across all six panels.
  negative: >
    missing or blank header row on any enhanced panel; sort arrows on the
    no-scripts panel; filter box on the default or class-form panels;
    table clipped by the page edge (every table scrolls inside its own
    frame); occluded, blurred or struck-through cell text; neon glow;
    light background; more or fewer than six labeled panels; watermark;
    lorem ipsum; invented nav bars, buttons or pagination not described.

  style: >
    Flat UI spec sheet, minimal-tech aesthetic, restrained single-accent
    palette, crisp 12px card radius, hairline borders, generous negative
    space. Reads as a panel from a design-system guide, not a dashboard
    screenshot.

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-table/sem-table-primary-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-table/sem-table-sticky-long-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-table/sem-table-comparison-wide-render-390.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-table-live/filter-1280.png
    role: reference

output:
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024

requirements:
  panels:
    - id: sortable
      visible:
        - caption and legible small-caps header labels
        - neutral up/down affordance on every sortable header
        - active header: accent label + single filled arrow, rows reordered
      must_never:
        - show a filter box or chrome bar on the default panel
        - leave the active sort state ambiguous
    - id: filter
      visible:
        - chrome bar with labelled search input and status "3 rows"
        - plain header labels without sort affordances
      must_never:
        - drop the status text
        - add sort arrows
    - id: sticky
      visible:
        - fixed-height table frame with internal vertical scrollbar mid-way
        - header row pinned and fully legible over scrolled body rows
      must_never:
        - scroll the header away with the body
        - show a page-level scrollbar doing the scrolling
    - id: comparison
      visible:
        - first column pinned with surface background + right hairline
        - body columns sliding under the pinned edge, clipped mid-glyph
        - internal horizontal scrollbar under the body
      must_never:
        - hide the first column
        - let the table overflow its card or the page
    - id: class-form
      visible:
        - pixels identical to the sortable panel
      must_never:
        - differ visually from the element form
    - id: no-scripts
      visible:
        - plain authored table: headers as plain text, authored row order
        - no chrome, no arrows, no scrollbar
      must_never:
        - hide any authored row or header
        - render interactive chrome

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    header-legibility:
      weight: 0.25
      description: >
        Every enhanced panel shows a real header row with legible column
        labels — the sort arrows ride ON the labels, never replace them.
      fail_signals:
        - blank or missing header band on an enhanced panel
        - header text occluded by arrows or chrome
    sort-affordance:
      weight: 0.2
      description: >
        Sort state reads at a glance: neutral affordance on idle sortable
        headers, accent label + single filled arrow on the active one, and
        the body order matching the claimed sort.
      fail_signals:
        - arrows on the no-scripts panel
        - active header indistinguishable from idle ones
        - body order contradicting the active sort
    sticky-and-containment:
      weight: 0.25
      description: >
        Sticky panel: header pinned over a mid-scrolled body with an
        internal scrollbar. Comparison panel: first column pinned while
        others slide under it, everything inside its frame — no page-level
        scrollbar anywhere.
      fail_signals:
        - header scrolled away on the sticky panel
        - first column missing on the comparison panel
        - a full-page scrollbar or clipped-by-page-edge table
    mode-coverage:
      weight: 0.2
      description: >
        Six labeled panels, each matching its caption; class-form pixels
        equal to the element form; the no-scripts panel carries zero
        interactive chrome.
      fail_signals:
        - wrong count of labeled panels
        - class-form panel differing from the element-form panel
        - chrome or arrows on the no-scripts panel
    theme-fidelity:
      weight: 0.1
      description: >
        Dark minimal-tech palette (#0f172a bg, #60a5fa accent), hairline
        borders, mono uppercase captions, consistent card rhythm.
      fail_signals:
        - light background or clashing accent hues
        - inconsistent panel sizing or caption style
  reject_if:
    - any enhanced panel has a missing or blank header row
    - any cell text is occluded, blurred, or struck through
    - a table is clipped by the page edge instead of scrolling inside its frame
    - the no-scripts panel shows interactive chrome
